{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gaudy-working-mantaray","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nComplete ADR 0098 for LLM execution after the command/store cutover. Many LLM operations currently call `LLMConfig.from_env()` independently, even though `LLMRuntime`, `ProviderSession`, gate config scoping, and snapshot composition already exist.\n\nThe goal is one behavior-bearing snapshot/context per public operation, not deletion of a legitimate top-level composition convenience. Ambient compatibility may remain only at an explicitly approved boundary and must delegate to the central composer.\n\n## Work\n\n- Derive a focused LLM config projection from the existing snapshot/schema/provenance; pair it with existing non-serializable `LLMRuntime`.\n- Thread that context through gate/workflow/runner entry points so subcalls inherit operation policy rather than re-resolving it.\n- Preserve ProviderSession/provider-native auth, budgets, cache/output/retry behavior, tracing, and secret exclusions.\n- Add consumer-level metamorphic tests covering multi-step runs and failure/retry paths.\n- Delete the shadow switch/function and migrated ambient-resolution branches after parity; tighten the existing ownership gate and documentation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each public CLI, MCP, and Python LLM/gate operation composes one snapshot/context; every subcall and workflow step receives its projection/runtime without rereading environment/files/CWD.\n- [ ] Mutating model/provider class, timeout, retry, cache, headers, tracing, or repository settings after composition cannot change an in-progress multi-step run; the next operation observes the mutation.\n- [ ] Explicit supplied config/snapshot stays authoritative, and missing/conflicting decision-bearing provider/auth composition fails before an external call without anonymous/cross-provider fallback.\n- [ ] `LLMRuntime` and `ProviderSession` remain the live-auth and provider-resource owners; no secret/live capability enters snapshot bytes, fingerprints, repr, logs, exceptions, or schemas.\n- [ ] `emit_shadow_snapshot`, its migration switch, diagnostic-only production call sites, and migrated below-boundary `LLMConfig.from_env` branches are deleted. Any retained `from_env` public composition wrapper delegates once to the central composer and is structurally allowlisted by exact symbol/rationale.\n- [ ] The ownership gate fails on synthetic direct/aliased ambient reloads and carries zero post-cutover legacy exceptions.\n- [ ] Consumer-level metamorphic tests plus focused LLM/provider/cache/fallback/workflow suites, default suite, lint, typecheck, complexity, and module-size gates pass; docs and ADR 0098 describe the authoritative state rather than shadow mode.","id":"ec44-b572-1067-4c52","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["configuration","llm","cutover"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Make OperationSnapshot authoritative for LLM operations and retire shadow resolution"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788026461495530271,"uuid":"b8d4b408-91d7-4e70-afba-e4c18158b8eb"}